Disables the two fixes this pin needs off together, both for a frozen entry
of a batch the brake held for its other paths (§8.1, §8.2). As before
bd63aa0, reconsider() takes a path's Frozen entries along with the
ChangedUnderneath ones it is asked for, so a scan or a commit at a frozen
path thaws its entry while the folder is still paused. As before 20a7504,
admit() no longer joins an entry whose own batch is still held to that held
item, so the entry meets the brake alone, passes, and is wanted. No
invariant sees an entry committed while its batch is held: I5 checks the
held item, which a frozen entry is never in. The two seeds in 0 to 9,999
that fail with this patch do so through I4's check of a copy under a
directory displaced twice, so the patch names unit tests: the one that
replaced this pin's seed, which fails with either fix disabled alone, and
bd63aa0's own.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_frozen_entry_of_a_held_batch_is_wanted_only_by_approve
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::frozen_entries_wait_for_unpause_through_scans_and_commits

